SakuraMoon iREPA frozen PE-Spatial teacher — vendored source notice
===================================================================

This package vendors a minimal, frozen-only subset of the Perception
Encoder (PE) vision encoder from:

  Repository : facebookresearch/perception_models
  Commit     : 3e352cca660658d4b5c90f42a7808b11469e4c66
  License    : Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE.PE in this directory)
  Copyright  : Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.

Vendored files (upstream path -> local path):
  core/vision_encoder/rope.py   -> rope.py        (copied byte-for-byte verbatim)
  core/vision_encoder/pe.py     -> pe_vision.py   (vision-encoder classes only)
  core/vision_encoder/config.py -> config.py      (PEConfig + B16-512 entry)

Deliberately NOT vendored (per the iREPA Phase 3 dependency policy):
  text/PLM towers, tokenizer, video/data/eval code, requirements.txt,
  and the huggingface_hub checkpoint fetcher.

Fidelity (verified by automated diff / AST comparison against the upstream
commit above):
  - rope.py: byte-for-byte identical (a 4-line provenance header prepended).
  - pe_vision.py: every vendored class (LayerScale, AttentionPooling,
    SelfAttention, ResidualAttentionBlock, Transformer, VisionTransformer)
    is AST-identical to upstream, with the single exception of
    VisionTransformer.from_config (see below).  Only import re-basing,
    unused-import trimming, and whitespace normalization differ textually.
  - config.py: the PE-Core-B16-224 and PE-Spatial-B16-512 definitions are
    AST-identical to upstream; PEConfig fields are identical.

Documented changes to the copied code:
  - import paths re-based to sakuramoon.pe_spatial;
  - unused imports trimmed in pe_vision.py;
  - pe_vision.py drops the text tower / CLIP / fetch_pe_checkpoint;
  - VisionTransformer.from_config's pretrained path requires a local
    checkpoint_path (the huggingface_hub fetcher is intentionally not
    vendored, so a pretrained load with no local path fails closed);
  - config.py: the `output_dim: Optional[int]` annotation is written as
    `int | None` (identical type), and the `image_size` field default is
    the int `224`.  Upstream's source line `image_size: int = 224,` is
    parsed by Python as a 1-tuple default `(224,)` (a trailing-comma
    typo); every PE_VISION_CONFIG entry passes an explicit int image_size,
    so the normalized default is behaviorally equivalent for all configs.

The teacher weights (PE-Spatial-B16-512.pt) are NOT part of this
repository; they are bound at runtime by the asset contract in
src/sakuramoon/assets/pe_spatial.py (SHA256 fingerprint).
